      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=121104",
      "title": "America, the ‘arsenal of democracy,’ is now disarming the press",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/america-the-arsenal-of-democracy-is-now-disarming-the-press/",
      "published": "Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:05:41 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>In a radio address in December 1940, one year before the US entered World War II, Franklin D Roosevelt described America as “the arsenal of democracy”. Today, the guns are falling silent across the western front. Independent journalism, the lifeblood of an informed democracy, faces existential challenges, particularly in the US, writes Lionel Barber for World News Day.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/09/america-the-arsenal-of-democracy-is-now-disarming-the-press/\">America, the &#8216;arsenal of democracy,&#8217; is now disarming the press</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
